A||||1||JohnnyK||What is the oil pressure supposed to be?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||05-29-2000||08:01 PM||||My oil pressure usually hovers in betwwen the quarter and halfway mark, but sometimes drops to the quarter mark.. Is this ok? Or should I be really concerned.. At first it stays smack in the middle for awhile?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||05-29-2000||10:28 PM||||The first question is: L4 or V6.<P>But.....<BR>1.10 PSI/1000 RPM up to 45 PSI is considered normal.<P>2. 10 PSI at idle is acceptable.<P>3. A normal motor idles at about 15-20 PSI and is about 50 PSI by 2500 RPM.<P>4. The gauge is horrible inaccurate.<P>5. The fuel pressure switch is active above 4 PSI.<P>6. As the oil heats, the pressure will drop. All of the above are when the engine is warm.<P>7. A new or tight engine will idle at 20-35 and have as much as 60+ above 2500 RPM.<P>8. The GM spec:<P>L4 - 36-41 at 2000 RPM. Notice there is no idle PSI?<P>V6 - 10 PSI minimum at 500 RPM and 50-55 PSI minimum at 2000 RPM.||||reg||1
